{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1087", "sample_idx": 32, "model_name": "meta/llama-3.1-8b-instruct", "content": "the social network is a 2010 american biographical drama film directed by david fincher and written by jesse armstrong and the screenplay was also co-written by armstrong and shawn sloan. the film is based on the book \"the accidental billionaires\" by ben Mezrich which focuses on the founding of the social networking site facebook and the subsequent lawsuits it spawned.\n\nthe film stars jesse eisenberg as mark zuckerberg, the co-founder and ceo of facebook, along with justin timberlake as sean parker, the co-founder who helped zuckerberg launch the site, and andrew garfield as eduardo saverin, a close friend of zuckerberg's who invested in the site.\n\nthe film begins with a montage of the early days of facebook, showcasing its rapid growth and popularity. it then cuts to a college party where zuckerberg and his friends are shown to be social outcasts. zuckerberg is shown to be particularly intelligent and ambitious, and he begins to work on a new social networking site.\n\nthe film then cuts to a series of flashbacks that show the early days of facebook and the people who helped zuckerberg launch the site. it also shows the early days of the lawsuits that facebook would face, including a lawsuit filed by the winklevoss twins, who claim that zuckerberg stole their idea for a social networking site.\n\none of the standout aspects of the film is its portrayal of the relationships between the characters. the film shows how zuckerberg's relationship with his friends and family deteriorates as facebook becomes more successful. it also shows how sean parker and zuckerberg's relationship becomes increasingly complicated as the site's success grows.\n\nthe film also explores the theme of ambition and the lengths to which people will go to achieve their goals. zuckerberg is shown to be a complex character, driven by a desire to succeed and to prove himself to others. the film raises questions about the morality of his actions and whether he crossed the line in his pursuit of success.\n\nthe film's cinematography is also noteworthy, with a muted color palette and a focus on the characters' faces and body language. the score is also excellent, with a haunting soundtrack that perfectly captures the mood of the film.\n\noverall, the social network is a thought-provoking and engaging film that raises important questions about ambition, friendship, and the consequences of success. it is a must-see for anyone interested in the history of facebook and the people who helped shape its early days.\n\nrating: 4.5/5 stars\n\nrecommendation: the social network is a must-see for anyone interested in the history of facebook and the people who helped shape its early days. it is a thought-provoking and engaging film that raises important questions about ambition, friendship, and the consequences of success.", "logprobs": [{"token": "the", "logprob": -0.045232724}, {"token": " social", "logprob": -0.0016868184}, {"token": " network", "logprob": -7.6293654e-06}, {"token": " is", "logprob": -0.18040486}, {"token": " a", "logprob": -0.00012385078}, {"token": " ", "logprob": -0.32515162}, {"token": "201", "logprob": -2.9086643e-05}, {"token": "0", "logprob": -3.933899e-06}, {"token": " american", "logprob": -0.3342006}, {"token": " bi", "logprob": -0.0031711787}, {"token": "ographical", "logprob": -0.00043990472}, {"token": " drama", "logprob": -0.011117537}, {"token": " film", "logprob": -0.00057299406}, {"token": " directed", "logprob": -0.18416922}, {"token": " by", "logprob": -0.0021900972}, {"token": " david", "logprob": -0.009290322}, {"token": " fin", "logprob": -0.00041380903}, {"token": "cher", "logprob": -2.682173e-05}, {"token": " and", "logprob": -0.2561861}, {"token": " written", "logprob": -0.0026351034}, {"token": " by", "logprob": -3.3378547e-06}, {"token": " j", "logprob": -1.11709}, {"token": "esse", "logprob": -0.047023352